.TH WHISRSD 1 "2026-11-14" "whisrs 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
whisrsd \- whisrs dictation daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B whisrsd
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B whisrsd
is the background daemon for the whisrs dictation system. It manages audio
capture, transcription, window tracking, and text injection via a virtual
keyboard.
.PP
The daemon listens on a Unix domain socket for commands from the
.BR whisrs (1)
CLI client. It runs as a long-lived process, either standalone or as a
systemd or OpenRC user service.
.PP
On startup, the daemon:
.IP \(bu 2
Loads configuration from
.IR ~/.config/whisrs/config.toml ,
with the active config profile merged over it (see PROFILES)
.IP \(bu 2
Checks /dev/uinput access for virtual keyboard
.IP \(bu 2
Resolves the \fB[audio] device\fR input and logs which device it will record from
.IP \(bu 2
Auto-detects the active window manager/compositor
.IP \(bu 2
Initializes the selected transcription backend
.IP \(bu 2
Binds the Unix domain socket and begins accepting commands
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH STATE MACHINE
The daemon maintains one of five states:
.TP
.B idle
Waiting for a toggle command. No audio is being captured.
.TP
.B recording
Audio is being captured from the microphone. A second toggle or a cancel
command transitions out of this state.
.TP
.B transcribing
Audio has been sent to the transcription backend. The daemon is waiting
for results. Text is typed at the cursor as it becomes available.
.TP
.B synthesizing
Read-aloud: generating speech from the selected text.
.TP
.B speaking
Read-aloud: playing synthesized speech; a second speak or a cancel stops it.
.SH PROFILES
A config profile is a partial
.I config.toml
in
.IR ~/.config/whisrs/profiles/NAME.toml .
The active one is named on one line of
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/whisrs/active\-profile
(no file, or
.BR base :
the base config alone). At startup its tables merge over
.I config.toml
key by key, and any other value replaces the base one, before the
unknown\-key check and validation;
.I vocabulary.txt
merges after. API keys,
.BR [hotkeys] ,
.BR [[llm_commands]] ,
.B [[agents]]
and
.B [recording] dir
stay in the base: a profile's are ignored, with a warning. A profile that is
missing, not valid TOML, or does not load or validate over the base is
warned about and notified, and the daemon runs on the base.
.PP
.B whisrs profile
(or
.BR "[hotkeys] next_profile" ,
or the tray's Profile menu) switches: refused unless dictation, read\-aloud,
recordings and agent turns are idle, and when the profile would not load.
A switch to base is refused too while
.I config.toml
does not load. Otherwise the daemon writes the active name, notifies,
answers, and restarts on it: through its service when it runs as one
(systemd or OpenRC), else by starting itself again with the same arguments.
Either way a recording in progress is finalized first, and the restart
runs the binary installed now, so an upgrade takes effect. Until the restart,
anything that would start a dictation, command mode, a read\-aloud, a
recording or a job on one, or an agent turn is refused with
.BR "switching profile: try again in a moment" ,
and agent replies wait. When something started anyway, or the restart
fails, the previous name comes back and a notification says why. The tray's
Restart Daemon restarts the same way.
.SH TRANSCRIPTION BACKENDS
Set with
.BR "[general] backend" .
Streaming backends type the text while you speak; the others send the audio
when you stop.
.TP
.BR groq ", " deepgram ", " openai
Groq's Whisper API, and the REST APIs of Deepgram and OpenAI.
.TP
.BR deepgram\-streaming ", " openai\-realtime
Deepgram and OpenAI's Realtime API over a WebSocket. Streaming.
.TP
.B openai\-compatible\-realtime
A realtime server that speaks OpenAI's protocol, such as a local one.
Streaming.
.TP
.B local\-whisper
whisper.cpp on this machine (the
.B local\-whisper
build feature, on by default). Fully offline. Streaming, phrase by phrase;
batch when \fB[local\-whisper] segmentation\fR is \fBnone\fR.
.TP
.B asr\-sidecar
Any HTTP server, local or hosted (OpenRouter, for example), that takes
OpenAI's transcription request format at
.BR "[asr\-sidecar] url" :
WAV audio as multipart form data, answered with JSON whose
.B text
field is the transcript.
.TP
.BR local\-vosk ", " local\-parakeet
Placeholders for native backends not built yet.
.SH SOCKET
The daemon creates a Unix domain socket at:
.PP
.RS
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/whisrs.sock
.RE
.PP
If
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
is not set, falls back to:
.PP
.RS
.IR /tmp/whisrs\-<uid>.sock
.RE
.PP
The socket is readable and writable by its owner only (mode 0600).
The protocol uses length-prefixed JSON messages (4-byte big-endian length
header followed by a JSON body).
.PP
On startup, the daemon checks for and removes stale sockets from previous
instances. If another daemon is already running, it exits with an error.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT
Graceful shutdown. The socket file is removed before exit.
.TP
.B SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown (when run as a systemd service).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Controls log verbosity. Examples:
.BR info ,
.BR debug ,
.BR "whisrs=debug" .
Default is
.BR info .
.TP
.B WHISRS_GROQ_API_KEY
Groq API key. Overrides the config file value.
.TP
.B WHISRS_OPENAI_API_KEY
OpenAI API key. Overrides the config file value.
.TP
.B WHISRS_DEEPGRAM_API_KEY
Deepgram API key. Overrides the config file value.
.TP
.B WHISRS_ASR_SIDECAR_API_KEY
Bearer token for an
.B asr\-sidecar
server. Overrides the config file value.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Socket directory.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Configuration directory.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Used to detect Wayland session for clipboard operations.
.TP
.B HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE
Used to detect Hyprland compositor for window tracking.
.TP
.B NIRI_SOCKET
Used to detect Niri compositor for window tracking.
.TP
.B SWAYSOCK
Used to detect Sway compositor for window tracking.
.TP
.B XDG_SESSION_TYPE
Used to detect X11 session for window tracking.
.TP
.B XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP
Used to detect GNOME and KDE, where window tracking is off: neither tells
whisrs which window has focus.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/whisrs/config.toml
Configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/whisrs/profiles/NAME.toml
Config profiles (see PROFILES).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/whisrs/active\-profile
The active profile's name (defaults to
.IR ~/.local/state/whisrs/active\-profile ).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/whisrs.sock
IPC socket.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/whisrs/recovery/
Audio recovery files saved on transcription failure (the newest 10 are
kept);
.B whisrs transcribe\-recovery
transcribes one.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/whisrs/recordings/
Recordings and their transcripts, one folder per recording. Override with
.B [recording] dir
in
.IR config.toml .
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the daemon in the foreground with debug logging:
.PP
.RS
RUST_LOG=debug whisrsd
.RE
.PP
Run the daemon in the background:
.PP
.RS
whisrsd &
.RE
.PP
Enable as a systemd user service:
.PP
.RS
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now whisrs.service
.RE
.PP
Enable as an OpenRC user service:
.PP
.RS
rc\-update \-\-user add whisrs default && rc\-service \-\-user whisrs start
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR whisrs (1)
